<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · site</p><h1 class="enc-title">Wola</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Wola is an area on the western outskirts of historic <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/warsaw">Warsaw</a>, now a district of the city. In the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polish-lithuanian-commonwealth">Polish-Lithuanian Commonwealth</a>, the field of Wola was the site of royal elections. The king was chosen there by the entire <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/szlachta">szlachta</a> nobility in mass elections, a distinctive feature of the Commonwealth's <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/elective-monarchy">elective monarchy</a>.</p></div>
